{"Title":"An Act requiring tax return disclosure to appear on a presidential primary ballot","BillNumber":"S434","DocketNumber":"SD617","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"RLR0","Name":"Rebecca L. Rausch","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RLR0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T13:54:36.033"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RLR0","Name":"Rebecca L. Rausch","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RLR0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T13:54:36.0333333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S434/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Rausch, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 434) of Rebecca L. Rausch for legislation to require tax return disclosure to appear on a presidential primary ballot.  Election Laws.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 28 of chapter 53 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following new paragraph:- The state secretary shall not place on the presidential primary ballot the name of any candidate who has not, at least sixty days in advance of the primary date, made public and readily available the candidate’s federal income tax returns, as defined in section 6103(b)(1) of the United States internal revenue code, for the immediately previous four years. The state secretary may promulgate regulations to implement this paragraph. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J15","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J15"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}